        "content": {
          "content_type": "text",
          "parts": [
            "Yes — I can explain **how you can check for spy cameras** using simple methods and tools. I cannot scan your room directly, but I can guide you step-by-step.\n\n---\n\n# ✅ **How to Detect a Hidden (Spy) Camera**\n\n## **1. Physical Inspection (Most Important)**\nLook carefully at common hiding spots:\n- **Smoke alarms**\n- **Air vents**\n- **Small holes** in walls or ceilings\n- **Picture frames**\n- **Clocks**\n- **USB chargers**\n- **Lamps**\n- **Mirrors** (two-way mirrors)\n\n**Tip:** Spy cameras must have a **tiny pinhole lens** (often black and circular).\n\n---\n\n## **2. Use Your Phone Flashlight**\nTurn off the lights and shine your phone flashlight slowly around the room.\n\n➡️ Camera lenses reflect light like a tiny **glowing dot**.\n\nMove the light slowly and check:\n- Walls  \n- Power outlets  \n- Decorations  \n- Electronics  \n\n---\n\n## **3. Use Your Phone Camera to Detect Infrared (IR)**\nMany hidden cameras use IR LEDs for night vision.\n\n### **How to test**\n1. Turn off the lights.\n2. Open your phone camera.\n3. Point it around suspicious objects.\n\n➡️ If you see **small glowing purple/white dots**, that may be an IR light from a hidden camera.\n\n(Front cameras on many phones detect IR better.)\n\n---\n\n## **4. Use a Wi-Fi Scanner App**\nHidden Wi-Fi cameras often appear as devices on your network.\n\n### Apps you can use:\n- **Fing**\n- **Network Analyzer**\n\nLook for devices like:\n- Unknown IP cameras  \n- “IPCam”\n- “ESP_XXXX”\n- “Camera_XXXX”\n- Strange MAC addresses\n\n---\n\n## **5. Use an RF (Radio Frequency) Detector**\nIf someone is transmitting video wirelessly, a cheap RF detector can help.\n\nPrice: **$15–$40** on Amazon or local electronics shops.\n\nIt can detect:\n- Wireless cameras  \n- Wi-Fi cameras  \n- Bluetooth trackers  \n- Audio bugs  \n\n---\n\n## **6. Check for Unusual Heat**\nSpy cameras produce small heat.\n\nUse your hand to feel for:\n- Warm spots on walls  \n- Warm USB chargers  \n- Warm power adapters\n\n---\n\n## **7. Listen for Clicking / Buzzing**\nSome cameras make small sounds when adjusting or powering up.\n\nPut your ear close to vents, clocks, or small electronics.\n\n---\n\n# If you want, I can guide you step-by-step **for your exact room**  \nTell me:\n- Is it a bedroom, bathroom, living room?\n- What items or suspicious objects you see?\n- Are you renting or in a condo?\n\nI’ll help you check each object carefully."
